      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "The video shows the object which attached at the hip bone.  Being attached to the hips is why you don't you don't see any movement on the Y axis, as your hips are not moving in the Y direction.   This is also the reason you are seeing the apparent lag.  When in 3 point tracking VRChat is updating your tracking space and hips separately from your camera, you can view this effect by looking down at your legs while rotating with the thumb stick.  Your legs will also lag behind.\n\nThere is some potential improvement we can make with the jitteryness of the hips update and will take that into consideration for future 3 point tracking improvements.",
